      },
      "message": "docs(process): PROCESS_VERSION and a pinned announcement so forks pick up process changes\n\nForks sync product code only at cut tags, so changes to AGENTS.md, the\nagents, the skills and the gate scripts never reached their agents until\nthe next release.\n\n- .claude/PROCESS_VERSION (now 1, tracked via .gitignore) - every PR that\n  changes a process file increments it.\n- AGENTS.md, fork rule: at the start of every session a fork compares its\n  PROCESS_VERSION with upstream/main's and, if behind, pulls just the\n  process files (the one exception to \"sync only to a cut tag\"; product\n  code stays on the tag). New rule: process PRs bump the version and are\n  announced on the pinned issue #681; release notes get a short \"Process\n  changes\" section.\n- PR-reviewer: a process-file PR without the bump is a requested change.\n- review-prs skill step 2d: the bump check and the #681 announcement on\n  merge.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
